<title>USA: McDonald's Corp Q1 net, revs, sales rise.</title>
<headline>McDonald's Corp Q1 net, revs, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			$  0.49		  $  0.42</p>
<p> Net			344,500		  301,600</p>
<p> Revs		   2,617,600		2,426,000</p>
<p> Systemwide sales   7,833,100		7,309,500</p>
<p>	 (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: During 1997 Q1, McDonald's repurchased 6.7 million common shares for about $300 million. Fewer shares outstanding resulted in the greater increase in net income per share than in net income.</p>
<p>Excluding a $16 million charge for the adoption of SFAS 121 in 1996 Q1 and the negative effect of weaker foreign currencies, 1997 Q1 net income per common share and net income increased 13 and 12 percent, respectively, from year earlier.</p>
<p>1997 Q1 had one less trading day compared with the prior year. This cut 1997 global results by about $0.01 a share.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
